  "text" : "A PyTorch dataset class has two functions.\nHow many samples and how do I get sample i.\nEverything else is the data loader's job.\nLen returns the number of samples.\nGetItem returns sample at index i.\nHere, the series are pre-computed into one tensor.\nSo getItem is just a slice.\nBecause you can index into the dataset,\nthe sampler owns the order.\nIt uses the length to make a random sequence of\nindices and calls getItem on each one.\nSo shuffling is free and\nThe validation split is just a list of indices.\nIf you've ever shuffled with torch.randperm and sliced batches by hand, you already wrote\nthis.\nrandperm is the sampler, the range step is the batcher, and the slice is getitem + colate.\nThis is called a map style dataset.\nYou use it when random access is cheap.\nIf you write these two functions first, the loader, the shuffle, and the split will come\nfor free."
}
